==Trivia== 
*The {{gold|Long Term Investment}} perk also applies to '''Diaz''' herself if she's elected minister and has the minister perk set to this perk.
*Due to both versions of [[Shen's Auction]]s refreshing on {{Season|m=LSP|d=1st}} and the new mayor taking office on {{Season|m=LSP|d=27th}}, the {{gold|Volume Trading}} perk only affects the '''{{red|next}}''' auction.
*'''Diaz'''{{'}}s Shopping Spree perk does {{red|not}} apply to {{NPCSprite|Kiara}}'s shop.
*The {{gold|Shopping Spree}} perk can be used to skip out on grinding certain items or to resell to the {{NPCSprite|Bazaar}} at a higher volume.
**Due to how long they take to grind out, {{Gamemode|Ironman}} players often buy {{Item|Dandelion}}s for {{Item|Flower Minion}} upgrades, as well as {{Item|Sponge}} and {{Item|Wet Sponge}} for {{Item|Sponge Armor}}, while this perk is active.
*'''Diaz'''{{'}}s old perk, {{gold|Barrier Street}}, is most likely a reference to Wall Street.
*Before her perks were overhauled, Diaz was by far the least elected mayor.
*Prior to 0.20.3, '''Diaz''' was the only normal mayor to have {{green|2}} perks.
*'''Diaz''' holds the record for most time between elections, taking {{green|98 years}}.
